{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoF9uwJLZJ5kZABbjvPr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`TokenBucket` is in `ledgerkit/limiter.py`, with tests in `tests/test_limiter.py`. I committed both on `crew/1107-b985ad` as `2822600`. `python3 -m pytest -q` gives 20 passed, which covers the existing money tests and the new ones.\n\nWhat the new tests check:\n- **Basics:** the bucket starts full, a failed `try_acquire` takes nothing, and `wait_time` is pure.\n- **Refill:** refill is capped at capacity, and a backwards clock adds and removes nothing while later refill continues from the new time.\n- **Validation:** `ValueError` is raised for bad `rate`, `capacity` and `n` in both methods.\n- **Exact wait:** over 5000 cycles with rates 0.1, 3 and 7, at clock starts 0 and 12345.678, waiting exactly `wait_time(n)` from empty always lets `try_acquire(n)` succeed.\n- **Threads:** 16 threads making 8000 attempts against 1000 tokens acquired exactly 1000 in total.\n\nTo keep floating point error from building up, balances are exact `Fraction`s, and a lock guards every method.\n\n**Tolerance:** the clock reading itself is a float, so `(now + w) - now` can come out slightly short of `w`. To absorb that, the code treats a balance within 1e-6 tokens of `n` as enough. In practice a request can succeed up to 1e-6 tokens early."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_read_input_tokens":35371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":188},"output_tokens":491,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d124c459-3848-45d6-b7a7-f66ed523152d","uuid":"d4a85c27-545f-4883-aca2-8957c24b636e","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:22:53.267Z","request_id":"req_01